# =============================================================================
# 020-geckoview-lite-no-glean.patch — PyreVixen: GeckoView Lite, no Glean,
# no Sentry, no Adjust, no crash submission
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
#   1. GeckoView Lite: build against the non-Omni GeckoView artifact, which
#      excludes the Glean native library baked into geckoview-*-omni.
#   2. Removes the Glean SDK, Sentry, Adjust and InstallReferrer dependencies.
#   3. Guts the telemetry/crash-report wiring: Glean is never initialized
#      (single choke point no-op'd), Sentry/Socorro crash services are
#      deleted, the metrics controller registers zero services, and the
#      CRASH_REPORTING / TELEMETRY / SENTRY_TOKEN / ADJUST_TOKEN build flags
#      are forced off.
#
#
# VERIFIED AGAINST: FIREFOX-ANDROID_158_0_RELEASE (2026-10-14).
#   * GeckoView Lite is REAL and is selected by the mozconfig flag
#     --enable-geckoview-lite: mobile/android/moz.configure:81
#       set_config("MOZ_ANDROID_GECKOVIEW_LITE", True, when="--enable-geckoview-lite")
#     consumed by android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/build.gradle
#     computeArtifactId(): without the flag the artifact is geckoview[-channel]-omni
#     (Omni = includes Glean native, per Firefox source docs "GeckoView
#     Architecture": the default `geckoview` build "does not contain such
#     libraries" and "is similarly dubbed Lite in the codebase").
#     => There is NO source hunk for Lite: a source patch cannot set a mozconfig
#     flag. The fork's CI mozconfig MUST contain:
#         ac_add_options --enable-geckoview-lite
#   * There is NO buildSrc/src/main/java/Gecko.kt or Dependencies.kt in this
#     tree (the first draft targeted files that do not exist), and
#     fenix/app/build.gradle is Groovy, not .kts. The real dependency lines
#     removed here are fenix/app/build.gradle: service-glean (project dep),
#     libs.mozilla.glean, libs.mozilla.glean.forUnitTests, the
#     org.mozilla.telemetry.glean-gradle-plugin application, lib-crash-sentry
#     (project dep), libs.sentry, libs.adjust, libs.installreferrer.
#   * The only Glean.initialize call site in the app is
#     GleanHelper.initializeGlean (components/GleanHelper.kt:64), called from
#     FenixApplication.maybeInitializeGlean(). No-op'ing it kills all Glean
#     init. (Glean cannot upload without initialize(); uploadEnabled defaults
#     to false.)
#   * Sentry: Analytics.isSentryEnabled() (components/Analytics.kt:200) gated
#     the SentryService block; both are deleted here, as is the
#     MozillaSocorroService block, the GleanCrashReporterService telemetry
#     service, the ExperimentDataRuntimeTagProvider (Nimbus enrollment tags),
#     and the Glean/Adjust/InstallReferrer/usage-reporting entries in the
#     MetricController service list.
#   * Settings.isTelemetryEnabled default true -> false (utils/Settings.kt).
#
# DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM THE FIRST DRAFT
#   * The first draft's buildSrc hunks are dropped: those files do not exist.
#   * Beyond dependency removal, this patch also deletes the init/call sites
#     (the first draft left them as best-effort comments), and additionally
#     removes Adjust + InstallReferrer (third-party attribution telemetry the
#     first draft missed).
#
# CONFIDENCE
#   * All hunks in THIS patch: CONFIDENT — every removed line was copied
#     verbatim from the 158.0 tree and the patch was verified with
#     `git apply --check`.
#   * REQUIRED FOLLOW-UP (first CI build, cannot be done by patch): deleting
#     the Glean SDK + glean-gradle-plugin stops generation of
#     org.mozilla.fenix.GleanMetrics.*, which 145 files reference
#     (rg -l "GleanMetrics\." fenix/app/src/main/java | wc -l → 145), and
#     76 files import mozilla.telemetry.glean.*. Every one of those references
#     must be deleted; the compile errors are the checklist:
#         rg -l "GleanMetrics\.|mozilla\.telemetry\.glean" fenix/app/src/main/java
#     Also: com.adjust.sdk.* (AdjustMetricsService.kt, AdjustSdkController.kt,
#     AdjustThirdPartySharingController.kt), com.android.installreferrer.*
#     (DefaultInstallReferrerClient.kt, InstallReferrerClientWrapper.kt, ...),
#     and the secret-settings Glean debug tools
#     (debugsettings/gleandebugtools/). The GleanMetrics-free tree is the
#     definition of done for this patch.
#   * Gecko-side telemetry prefs (toolkit.telemetry.*, datareporting.*,
#     toolkit.crashreporter.*) remain enforced via config/default-prefs.js,
#     which is outside the patches/ directory.
# =============================================================================

